# .NET / Blazor

## API
- Prefer Minimal API endpoints; group by feature (Vertical Slice), not giant controllers.
- Keep DTOs contracted and shared; do not redefine domain models in the UI layer.
- Validate at the boundary; return deterministic errors (IT messages if product already does).

## Razor / UI
- No heavy domain logic in `.razor` pages — extract reusable components / services.
- Pages orchestrate; Core/Server owns parsing, COM, CIP, business rules.
- Prefer existing design tokens/theme over inventing a second visual system.

## General
- Target the solution's TFM; do not bump SDK/package majors without KB + tests.
- Keep secrets and plant paths out of git; use Samples/fixtures for demos.
- Run the repo's gate (`dotnet test` / smoke) before claiming done.

## KB (this repo)

- Preserve hub-orchestration boundaries; avoid dumping plant IP into public commits.
